      </div>

    <div class="typo-feature-body split feature-sub">
      <h3 class="rule-title" id="typo-title">Type styles as one token.</h3>
      <div class="typo-feature-text">
        <p>A type style is a set of properties: family, size, weight,
          line-height, tracking. <code>typography()</code> makes it one token,
          the W3 <code>typography</code> composite, so it sits in a scope like
          everything else. Its fields are tracked in the graph like any rule: a
          <code>ref()</code> carries the whole style,
          <code>ref('type.heading.fontSize')</code> reads one field. Renderers
          write a variable per field plus a CSS class for the browser, and a
          <code>$type: 'typography'</code> token for W3 Design Tokens.</p>
      </div>

      <Folder>
        <Sheet name="code" label="Code"><Code is:raw>type.set('heading', typography({
  fontFamily:    ref('fonts.serif'),
  fontSize:      rem(2.5),
  fontWeight:    '700',
  lineHeight:    1,
  letterSpacing: '-0.02em',
}));

// a variant reads the rest from its base, live
type.set('hero', variant(
  ref('type.heading'),
  { fontSize: rem(4) },
));

// one field, anywhere
callout.set('size', ref('type.heading.fontSize'));</Code></Sheet>
        <Sheet name="result" label="Result" front>
          <figure class="typo-stage">
            <div class="typo-sample typo-sample--heading">Type styles travel whole.</div>
            <div class="typo-sample typo-sample--hero">Variants follow.</div>
          </figure>
        </Sheet>
      </Folder>
    </div>
  </section>

