          space decides the path: <code>rgb</code> goes straight through the
          cube, <code>lab</code> and <code>oklab</code> follow perceptual lines,
          <code>lch</code>, <code>oklch</code> and <code>hsl</code> rotate around
          the hue. Same two colors, very different middles. Any
          <code>color-mix()</code> space works, and the CSS renderer writes the
          matching <code>color-mix()</code>.</p>
